{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 35,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Of David. Contend with my opponents, O LORD; fight against those who fight against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take up Your shield and buckler; arise and come to my aid.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Draw the spear and javelin against my pursuers; say to my soul: “I am your salvation.”",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May those who seek my life be disgraced and put to shame; may those who plan to harm me be driven back and confounded.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May they be like chaff in the wind, as the angel of the LORD drives them away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May their path be dark and slick, as the angel of the LORD pursues.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For without cause they laid their net for me; without reason they dug a pit for my soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May ruin befall them by surprise; may the net they hid ensnare them; may they fall into the hazard they created.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then my soul will rejoice in the LORD and exult in His salvation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All my bones will exclaim, “Who is like You, O LORD, who delivers the afflicted from the aggressor, the poor and needy from the robber?”",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hostile witnesses come forward; they make charges I know nothing about.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They repay me evil for good, to the bereavement of my soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet when they were ill, I put on sackcloth; I humbled myself with fasting, but my prayers returned unanswered.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I paced about as for my friend or brother; I was bowed down with grief, like one mourning for his mother.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But when I stumbled, they assembled in glee; they gathered together against me. Assailants I did not know slandered me without ceasing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like godless jesters at a feast, they gnashed their teeth at me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How long, O Lord, will You look on? Rescue my soul from their ravages, my precious life from these lions.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then I will give You thanks in the great assembly; I will praise You among many people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let not my enemies gloat over me without cause, nor those who hate me without reason wink in malice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they do not speak peace, but they devise deceitful schemes against those who live quietly in the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They gape at me and say, “Aha, aha! Our eyes have seen!”",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O LORD, You have seen it; be not silent. O Lord, be not far from me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Awake and rise to my defense, to my cause, my God and my Lord!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Vindicate me by Your righteousness, O LORD my God, and do not let them gloat over me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them not say in their hearts, “Aha, just what we wanted!” Let them not say, “We have swallowed him up!”",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May those who gloat in my distress be ashamed and confounded; may those who exalt themselves over me be clothed in shame and reproach.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May those who favor my vindication shout for joy and gladness; may they always say, “Exalted be the LORD who delights in His servant’s well-being.”",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.35.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then my tongue will proclaim Your righteousness and Your praises all day long.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
